{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too","id":1130240,"title":"Willpower cost for Cruac too","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-17T07:22:33-07:00","id":1130240,"title":"Willpower cost for Cruac too","content":"Hello. I always have believed Theban sorcery rituals are more expensive than Cruac ones (because vitae is far easier than replenish than WP), something Strix Chronicles didn't bother fixing. <br /> So I houseruled all rituals require a WP point in order to establish communion with the divine (whatever is God, the Crone, the Beast, etc...), plus the offering demanded in exchange (blood for Cruac, material components for Theban). <br /> What do you guys think? Is it balanced?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T09:59:36-07:00","id":1130333,"title":"","content":"Personally I found Theban Sorcery to be more expensive due to the fact that they have to buy material components for almost every spell and said components are not things you can just pick up at a Walmart or local strip mall while with Cruac just snatch anyone off the street and you have what you need. Insofar as balance is concerned, I don't think it will work but my balance concerns stems from a different area. Ulltimately you are the one who is going to have to answer that. If your players and your NPCs routinely throw around Cruac more often than Theban, it will probably work as a balancing feature. If they aren't used often anyway or willpower is easy to replenish, it won't impact anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T11:39:45-07:00","id":1130375,"title":"","content":"Part of the cost for Cruac is not so much it how much it costs to use, but how much it costs to <i>know</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:23:40-07:00","id":1130434,"title":"","content":"That is, I think the reduction in maximum humanity balances the willpower cost.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:39:34-07:00","id":1130492,"title":"","content":"I believes that Cruac is costly in the fact of how much vitae it actually costs. The price of a ritual just goes higher with the strength of the ritual while the a miracle always has the same flat cost of one willpower.<br /> <br /> I also typically run the sacrament as obtainable by the Sanctum itself for the more powerful or costly requirements; for the most dangerous rituals this might require justification, but the Miracle won't be outright impissible to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:51:53-07:00","id":1130505,"title":"","content":"Most players don\u00b4t get Cruac higher than 3, so the cost in blood or the humanity cap doesn\u00b4t hinder them a lot. Willpower, however, is near impossible to replenish unless indulging their Vices or Virtues in a meaningful way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:29:08-07:00","id":1130537,"title":"","content":"First thing first, is the blood sorcery book used, and if then it might be worth having blood magic, either one. Second this is a thing other people can't answer really, because how often you get back willpower depends on the players and ST around each table, how often is vice and virtue played out, meaningful interactions with touchstones, surrendering in combat etc etc and how often do the group remember to give out the willpower points ( my group forgets all the time!). And more , how easy and common is Blood and Vitae in the setting / group-play, how much time is spent hunting, how easy is it to get blood and is every hunting scene played out or just a dice roll with a &quot;successes in blood points&quot; kinda a way. And how much time/resources is needed to get the sacraments for Theban, is it a quest, a small dice roll, or just hand-waving it... And more.<br /> <br /> So like using two 3 dot rituals is somewhere between really easy or extremely costly depending on play-style etc. I for one would say getting back willpower to have a ritual working is probably easier then needing more blood to sustain yourself that night. 1 or 2 extra blood for one ritual ain't such a big deal, it's like using another discipline that night. But those two 3 dot rituals, thats a dead human with everything that comes with that or an extremely long hunt for plenty of vessels to sustain all that 7 blood needed just tonight. Or she could have a scene playing out her dirge or mask, perhaps even during the nights ritual, and then hang out with one of her touchstones for one scene getting a plot hook or drama point, and the willpower points are back. <br /> <br /> Cruac also has that pesky humanity cost, and cap, which can be quite costly if you don't want your humanity that low. A dot of cruac is a detachment roll for humanity 4(?)<br /> <br /> So about balance, you need to look at your own group for it and ask yourself and discuss it with the players, how they feel about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:30:34-07:00","id":1130539,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that Willpower is meant to be as hard to gain as people are making it out here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On average, characters should regain a point of<br /> Willpower every few scenes, depending on how<br /> easily they fulfill their Vices. They\u2019ll be spending it<br /> quicker than that, but the diminishing resource<br /> until a character is exhausted is another part<br /> of the game, modeling the genre of increasingly<br /> tired and desperate investigators confronting<br /> the supernatural, making the full Willpower<br /> refreshes from Virtue special. A character<br /> shouldn\u2019t always fulfill their Virtue in a game ses-<br /> sion \u2014 once every few stories is enough in big<br /> dramatic moments. We removed the risk limit<br /> from Vice to allow Storytellers to keep charac-<br /> ters \u201ctopped up\u201d in service to the game. If your<br /> players over-spend, give them easy opportuni-<br /> ties to fulfill Vice. Keep the small gains trickling<br /> in to prevent players from sitting on Willpower<br /> to their characters\u2019 detriment, and look for the<br /> right point to showcase Virtue. </div> </div> </div>GMC pg. 153<br /> <br /> There's more to the sidebar. They talk about the design philosophy of Willpower in 2e. It's a sidebar I wish had been kept in CofD. You can also regain Willpower in scenes doing other things, whereas Vitae tends to require scenes dedicated to gathering it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1692,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","user":"Maina","date":". 08-17-2017, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:39:19-07:00","id":1130546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1130539#post1130539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that Willpower is meant to be as hard to gain as people are making it out here.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree here. My group usually has an opposite problem, not enough dice rolls as opposite to not enough willpower points <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T17:59:13-07:00","id":1130627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1130505#post1130505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most players don\u00b4t get Cruac higher than 3, so the cost in blood or the humanity cap doesn\u00b4t hinder them a lot. Willpower, however, is near impossible to replenish unless indulging their Vices or Virtues in a meaningful way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rules as written, you get willpower back after sleeping, plus what others posted above. Your perception of how hard willpower is to regain is off base.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T18:29:13-07:00","id":1130635,"title":"","content":"Vampires don't get Willpower back by sleeping, since they don't sleep in a way that refreshes them the way mortals to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T00:49:28-07:00","id":1130741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1130627#post1130627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rules as written, you get willpower back after sleeping, plus what others posted above. Your perception of how hard willpower is to regain is off base.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires don't get willpower back from the daysleep because it is never restful. The only ways for a vampire to get willpower back is: defending their attachment to a touchstone, their Dirge, and their Mask.<br /> <br /> I believe vampire alone is this way and it was supposed to make it in the 2e vampire book, but it didn't for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T01:22:25-07:00","id":1130746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1130635#post1130635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires don't get Willpower back by sleeping, since they don't sleep in a way that refreshes them the way mortals to.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1130741#post1130741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires don't get willpower back from the daysleep because it is never restful. The only ways for a vampire to get willpower back is: defending their attachment to a touchstone, their Dirge, and their Mask.<br /> <br /> I believe vampire alone is this way and it was supposed to make it in the 2e vampire book, but it didn't for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>And since it didn't make it to the 2e Vampire book, and it wasn't included in errata, there's really nothing to indicate that vampires don't get willpower back from sleep.<br /> <br /> Basically, you're citing rules that don't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T02:14:12-07:00","id":1130748,"title":"","content":"The absence of rules doesn't indicate the prevelence of said rule.<br /> But no, you don't get willpower from sleep as a vampire, never had. And Rose has pointed it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/52522-regaining-willpower?p=53362#post53362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires don't get Willpower back from resting by default. One of the things Willpower represents is strength of self, parallel to Humanity. You get it for affirming who you are, who you pretend to be, and what you're connected to. Being a vampire is spiritually exhausting, and you have to emphasize those things in order to regain what normal people gain from rest.<br /> <br /> I say that with the following caveats:<ul><li>When significant downtime has passed (say, you skip a week of in-character time, or conclude a significant piece of your story and pick up later), it's reasonable to just refill everyone's Willpower, making the assumption they've been out interacting with their Anchors while off-screen.</li> <li>I don't think it does any harm to allow Kindred to regain Willpower from rest, it's just not the default for the reasons I expressed.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T02:34:16-07:00","id":1130753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1130741#post1130741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe vampire alone is this way and it was supposed to make it in the 2e vampire book, but it didn't for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was included by virtue of there not being a rule about vampires gaining Willpower through sleep. Remember, the 2E core books are stand alone and not just templates added to the GMCRU or CofD core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T06:30:15-07:00","id":1130792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1130753#post1130753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was included by virtue of there not being a rule about vampires gaining Willpower through sleep. Remember, the 2E core books are stand alone and not just templates added to the GMCRU or CofD core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I meant more of an explicit statement of it. I didn't know about that rule before I read what Rose wrote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T06:34:17-07:00","id":1130795,"title":"","content":"I also want to say that there are little rituals that elders can do every night that will refresh a willpower point. I can't remember the official name of them, but they were basically things the Elder did that reminded them of their time as a human.<br /> <br /> This rule came out in 1000 years of night, and I would say it probably wouldn't be too harmful to let younger characters do these rituals after some time being a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T09:25:38-07:00","id":1130858,"title":"","content":"Since the rule about <i>regaining</i> willpower does exist in a book and the rule explicitly stating that a vampire does <i>not</i> regain willpower does not exist in the book, I'm going to go with that interpretation.<br /> <br /> Interesting how when I brought up Rose's post about it before several people told me the rule effectively did not make the cut, and aren't saying anything this time.<br /> <br /> Also, it's a solution for the OP if he finds that vampires have too hard a time recovering willpower. Obv. willpower is a precious resource but I don't think it's supposed to be <i>that</i> precious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 08-18-2017, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T09:42:05-07:00","id":1130870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1130858#post1130858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting how when I brought up Rose's post about it before several people told me the rule effectively did not make the cut, and aren't saying anything this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if you meant me with this, but I wasn't saying that the rule itself didn't make the cut on the writing floor. I meant that I thought it was accidentally left out of the book. <br /> <br /> Of course. I have no issue with you using your own interpretation, but I did like the little rituals that a vampire could do to regain willpower, similar to a night's rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T10:15:01-07:00","id":1130877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1130870#post1130870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure if you meant me with this, but I wasn't saying that the rule itself didn't make the cut on the writing floor. I meant that I thought it was accidentally left out of the book.<br /> <br /> Of course. I have no issue with you using your own interpretation, but I did like the little rituals that a vampire could do to regain willpower, similar to a night's rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant literally no one in this thread. When I had previously cited Rose's post to say that vampires <i>can't</i> regain willpower from rest, several people took the time to inform me the rule didn't make the cut and didn't technically actually apply.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T12:51:21-07:00","id":1130931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1130877#post1130877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant literally no one in this thread. When I had previously cited Rose's post to say that vampires <i>can't</i> regain willpower from rest, several people took the time to inform me the rule didn't make the cut and didn't technically actually apply.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where did you cite and quote Rose? Cus I can't see it? The intent wasn't to have vampires sleep-regain willpower, it has been said they don't, it is not in the rules. And to be frank, I have not seen anyone defending the point that they are regaining, even though they are not.<br /> <br /> Even still. The rules for how vampires regain willpower is in the 2ed requiem corebook. Sleeping is absent by design. Rose has said so. Even if death of the author applies, nothing in the requiem corebook implies that sleeping should give willpower and the willpower from sleeping dilemma has been answered by the devs and talked about this topic more then once. <br /> <br /> So to be clear, vampires don't get willpower from sleeping by default. Every change to this, is a house-rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T10:12:55-07:00","id":1131331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1130931#post1130931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Where did you cite and quote Rose? Cus I can't see it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about a different thread from several months ago. Nothing I said in this thread implied it happened in this thread. I actually said &quot;I meant literally no one in this thread.&quot; So why would you keep referring to this thread to find what I was talking about?<br /> <br /> Anyway, since the rule is omitted completely, it's not necessarily a house rule so much as an interpretation of an omission. The book doesn't address it <i>at all</i>, but the CofD core rules say sleeping recovers willpower. So asking &quot;Do vampires do this too?&quot; is reasonable, as is deciding &quot;yes, they do this too.&quot; It's a valid interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 08-19-2017, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:41:58-07:00","id":1131446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1131331#post1131331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was talking about a different thread from several months ago. Nothing I said in this thread implied it happened in this thread. I actually said &quot;I meant literally no one in this thread.&quot; So why would you keep referring to this thread to find what I was talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I can read a thread, that's why I asked where? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, since the rule is omitted completely, it's not necessarily a house rule so much as an interpretation of an omission. The book doesn't address it <i>at all</i>, but the CofD core rules say sleeping recovers willpower. So asking &quot;Do vampires do this too?&quot; is reasonable, as is deciding &quot;yes, they do this too.&quot; It's a valid interpretation. </div> </div> </div>Okey if You want to follow that line, go ahead. But by the same logic, for example, werewolves should get beats for breaking points and all characters should switch aspirations after the scene because that's in Mage 2ed core.<br /> The omission of a statement is not the same as that statement should reasonable exist. It is left out from the book. Word by word, the paragraphs are identical in requiem 2ed and CofD-rulebook concerning what willpower does and how it's spent, except for two things. The first is a style change, in where they switched letters to digits (or vice versa) and the other is the addition of a sentence not there at all. That extra sentence is the willpower-sleep thing. Omission is not a valid argument, especially when there is nothing that indicates that it should apply. Extrapolating the rule here is clearly not applicable, the rule applies to different splats, in different books and where it was omitted the dev team has called it out and as well in this case, the dev team has called it out as well. And the consensus as far as i know it, and its faulty i give it that, is that vampires by default don't get willpower from sleep.<br /> <br /> However the sleep-willpower thing was a thing proposed in my Haven thread, that vampires sleeping in a Haven (merit) should regain willpower when sleeping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:55:33-07:00","id":1131455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/52522-regaining-willpower?p=53362#post53362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires don't get Willpower back from resting by default. One of the things Willpower represents is strength of self, parallel to Humanity. You get it for affirming who you are, who you pretend to be, and what you're connected to. Being a vampire is spiritually exhausting, and you have to emphasize those things in order to regain what normal people gain from rest.<br /> <br /> I say that with the following caveats:<ul><li>When significant downtime has passed (say, you skip a week of in-character time, or conclude a significant piece of your story and pick up later), it's reasonable to just refill everyone's Willpower, making the assumption they've been out interacting with their Anchors while off-screen.</li> <li>I don't think it does any harm to allow Kindred to regain Willpower from rest, it's just not the default for the reasons I expressed.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's the quote so the meaningless bickering can stop.<br /> <br /> There are people that believe in Word of God, and those that believe in the Death of the Author. The two will never agree, as this is a fundamentally incompatible difference in perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T16:32:18-07:00","id":1131502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1131455#post1131455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's the quote so the meaningless bickering can stop.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not like I've already quoted that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T18:26:26-07:00","id":1131543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1131455#post1131455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's the quote so the meaningless bickering can stop.<br /> <br /> There are people that believe in Word of God, and those that believe in the Death of the Author. The two will never agree, as this is a fundamentally incompatible difference in perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>The argument - which is not meaningless - is not over what Rose Bailey said. We all know what Rose said<i>.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T18:28:40-07:00","id":1131545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1131446#post1131446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I can read a thread, that's why I asked where?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I keep links for every thread I've ever posted to?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1131446#post1131446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okey if You want to follow that line, go ahead. But by the same logic, for example, werewolves should get beats for breaking points and all characters should switch aspirations after the scene because that's in Mage 2ed core.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bad argument and you should feel bad for making it because Mage 2ed core is the core book for Mage, whereas the Chronicles of Darkness core book is the core book for the CofD, which includes Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Promethean, Changeling, etc. While it is not <i>required</i> as the first edition core book was, <i>what it is</i> has not fundamentally changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 08-19-2017, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T18:42:52-07:00","id":1131554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too#post1130240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello. I always have believed Theban sorcery rituals are more expensive than Cruac ones (because vitae is far easier than replenish than WP), something Strix Chronicles didn't bother fixing.<br /> So I houseruled all rituals require a WP point in order to establish communion with the divine (whatever is God, the Crone, the Beast, etc...), plus the offering demanded in exchange (blood for Cruac, material components for Theban).<br /> What do you guys think? Is it balanced?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Don't you need a low Humanity score to learn Cruac, with the more powerful rituals needing you to be a borderline Draugr?<br /> <br /> Adding a willpower cost on top of that would make them ridiculously expensive, since you'd be in near constant risk of Frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T19:39:10-07:00","id":1131574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1131554#post1131554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Don't you need a low Humanity score to learn Cruac, with the more powerful rituals needing you to be a borderline Draugr?<br /> <br /> Adding a willpower cost on top of that would make them ridiculously expensive, since you'd be in near constant risk of Frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Knowing Cruac caps your Humanity at 10-Cruac, meaning maxing it out caps you at 5 Humanity.<br /> <br /> Learning Cruac is a Humanity sin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T21:04:51-07:00","id":1131598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1131574#post1131574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Knowing Cruac caps your Humanity at 10-Cruac, meaning maxing it out caps you at 5 Humanity.<br /> <br /> Learning Cruac is a Humanity sin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, I thought it maxed out at around 3 humanity or something like that.<br /> <br /> But 5 is above average for most stabilized vampires, so it doesn't sound like <i>too much</i> of a trade off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T21:26:52-07:00","id":1131607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1131545#post1131545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a bad argument and you should feel bad for making it because Mage 2ed core is the core book for Mage, whereas the Chronicles of Darkness core book is the core book for the CofD, which includes Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Promethean, Changeling, etc. While it is not <i>required</i> as the first edition core book was, <i>what it is</i> has not fundamentally changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Vampire: The Requiem is the corebook for Vampire: The Requiem. Chronicles of Darkness, despite sharing name with the collective franchise, is just the corebook for playing unaltered, non-Hunter humans. Any rules contained in Chronicles of Darkness is optional when playing Vampire: The Requiem because Vampire: The Requiem is standalone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T22:04:03-07:00","id":1131618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1131607#post1131607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Vampire: The Requiem is the corebook for Vampire: The Requiem. Chronicles of Darkness, despite sharing name with the collective franchise, is just the corebook for playing unaltered, non-Hunter humans. Any rules contained in Chronicles of Darkness is optional when playing Vampire: The Requiem because Vampire: The Requiem is standalone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is possible for me to disagree more with this statement than I already do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T22:33:34-07:00","id":1131623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1131543#post1131543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The argument - which is not meaningless - is not over what Rose Bailey said. We all know what Rose said<i>.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the argument seems to be over whether or not it's the official rule since it didn't 'make the cut', which is exactly what the latter half of my post was regarding.<br /> <br /> I simply added the quote again because for some reason a four post derail about *where* it was posted somehow seemed appropriate?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1131618#post1131618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it is possible for me to disagree more with this statement than I already do.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can disagree all you want, it doesn't change the fact that the Devs have repeatedly stated that the core for each line is intended to be standalone, containing all the rules required for play. Vampire does <i>not</i> contain rules about sleeping to regain Willpower, and the Dev has already come out and stated that they don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T12:02:47-07:00","id":1131820,"title":"","content":"Quoted from the V:tR2e corebook, emphasis mine: &quot;How to Use This Book: Welcome to Vampire: the Requiem, Second Edition. <b>Inside, you'll find a complete game</b>, ranging from core concepts of the world of the dead to descriptions of vampire city-states around the world. <b>You'll also find complete rules </b>for playing one of the Kindred&quot;. <br /> <br /> So, Resplendent Fire, how do you read these lines and then tell me that the rules in this book are NOT a complete game, and they AREN'T the complete rules? Because you seem to be arguing that it is necessary to apply rules from another book. This isn't a Dev statement that you can ignore, this is straight up the section in the book entitled &quot;How to Use This Book&quot;. So the Book says &quot;you don't need to use other rules&quot;, Devs have states &quot;you don't need to use other rules&quot;, Devs have states specifically &quot;you don't use this specific other rule&quot;, and you come out of this with the opinion that &quot;you need to use this specific other rule&quot;? You can play your own game like that if you think it makes your game better, no problem, but you can't go around telling people that it's a mandatory rule when it's pretty clearly not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T12:14:00-07:00","id":1131828,"title":"","content":"I never said they weren't a complete game, so if you could not attribute things to me that I never said that'd be splendid.<br /> <br /> I see people are seriously offended at the notion of allowing vampires to regain willpower from sleep though. It's funny when I took the opposite stance on this before I also had people lecturing me on how I was wrong, and how none of the people who did that have said one word in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T14:52:12-07:00","id":1131893,"title":"","content":"So... you're complaining that the people who opposed you in a previous thread aren't going out of their way to oppose you in this thread? A thread that, for all you know, they haven't even read yet?<br /> <br /> Why are you arguing against people who aren't even here instead of addressing the comments made in this thread?<br /> <br /> How does what different people said to you in a different thread have any bearing on this conversation?<br /> <br /> You've been needlessly hostile for several posts now because of, apparently, people who aren't even here. This doesn't make any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T17:51:07-07:00","id":1131965,"title":"","content":"Okay back on topic, the way blood Sorcery works, I find it funny that Ghouls are better potientially at Theban Sorcery then Vampires, but max out effectly at Cruac \u2022 unless they have a vampire will to bleed vitae for their rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T19:02:37-07:00","id":1131995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1131607#post1131607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Vampire: The Requiem is the corebook for Vampire: The Requiem. Chronicles of Darkness, despite sharing name with the collective franchise, is just the corebook for playing unaltered, non-Hunter humans. Any rules contained in Chronicles of Darkness is optional when playing Vampire: The Requiem because Vampire: The Requiem is standalone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That was the case with classic World of Darkness, in which there was no 'core' rule book shared among them.<br /> <br /> Chronicles is different. It even says in their respective books that the splats are templates to be applied to a character sheet after you finish their mortal write up.<br /> <br /> Unless I missed something during my read through?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1131965#post1131965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay back on topic, the way blood Sorcery works, I find it funny that Ghouls are better potientially at Theban Sorcery then Vampires, but max out effectly at Cruac \u2022 unless they have a vampire will to bleed vitae for their rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it funny that vampires (who refer to themselves as damned) have the power to use Theban Sorcery in the first place.<br /> <br /> How do you showcase a blood drinking corpse being able to wield biblical miracles and then claim their God is 'holy.'<br /> <br /> That's like a vampire brandishing a crucifix against a human! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-20-2017, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T02:10:31-07:00","id":1132126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1131995#post1131995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find it funny that vampires (who refer to themselves as damned) have the power to use Theban Sorcery in the first place.<br /> <br /> How do you showcase a blood drinking corpse being able to wield biblical miracles and then claim their God is 'holy.'<br /> <br /> That's like a vampire brandishing a crucifix against a human! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How do humans, born sinners and sinful in it's very existence in christian dogma, still able to be 'holy' and do Gods work in christian theology ?<br /> It's the same kind of hypocrisy that's inherent in every religion, just use the bits that support your claims and downplay the ones that don't. <br /> Don't really read scripture, listen to and appeal to authority for the 'truth' and the true way of theological practice.<br /> <br /> So well, the vampires of the Chapel and Spear say they have a holy mission, and use the will of God through them against the sinners and blasphemers and all that.<br /> L&amp;S is under the impression that humanity has lost it's spirituality, it's faith and must be tested and frightened back to God for their salvation. In their damned state, they still serve a holy mission, many in hope for redemption in the end.<br /> <br /> <br /> But back to the Ghoul thing. That's actually pretty funny that they would have less problem then most vampires with Theban sorcery over-all.<br /> However, the arbitrary &quot;don't spill blood&quot; thing ghouls can't do, i totally ignore cus i really can't see a reason. If a ghoul want's to take lethal damage to cut herself open and spill some extra vitae, why shouldn't she be able to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T02:15:16-07:00","id":1132129,"title":"","content":"Then you also have to add that ghouls are capable of manipulating their Vitae in order to force it through wounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T02:40:19-07:00","id":1132138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1132129#post1132129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you also have to add that ghouls are capable of manipulating their Vitae in order to force it through wounds.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah that's technically true, but I don't really see it as a far stretch to let the discipline use take care of that, like if you're using vitae to power a discipline, the vitae itself could concentrate itself around the wound and pour out together with the ghouls blood. I don't see that as a far stretch of the suspension of disbelief how vitae and blood works in vampire.<br /> <br /> Ergo, in my house-ruling, i get to keep the ghouls can't transfer vitae around and such, but still have (some) use for every discipline dot they buy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T04:05:36-07:00","id":1132153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1132129#post1132129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you also have to add that ghouls are capable of manipulating their Vitae in order to force it through wounds.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's like a drug addict choosing to go through detox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T06:49:16-07:00","id":1132193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1131995#post1131995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I missed something during my read through?</div> </div> </div> </div>You missed second edition. In 1E every book referred to the Blue Core which was the shared core between lines. That's gone now - seriously, look at the books.<br /> <br /> None of the 2E books (save maybe demon?) refer to the blue core for character creation or for anything else. They 100% contain all rules for their gameline, supplements notwithstanding. This was an intentional design decision.<br /> <br /> Note that no one is saying that they <i>can't</i> be used together, but using the existence of a Blue Book rule to support that the rule (which was intentionally omitted) should exist in vampire is fundamentally flawed, because there's no inherent reliance on the blue book anymore - it's not the 'core' for the gamelines and hasn't been since 1E.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:03:15-07:00","id":1132257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1132193#post1132193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You missed second edition. In 1E every book referred to the Blue Core which was the shared core between lines. That's gone now - seriously, look at the books.<br /> <br /> None of the 2E books (save maybe demon?) refer to the blue core for character creation or for anything else. They 100% contain all rules for their gameline, supplements notwithstanding. This was an intentional design decision.<br /> <br /> Note that no one is saying that they <i>can't</i> be used together, but using the existence of a Blue Book rule to support that the rule (which was intentionally omitted) should exist in vampire is fundamentally flawed, because there's no inherent reliance on the blue book anymore - it's not the 'core' for the gamelines and hasn't been since 1E.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, well that's a nice piece of information to have. Thank you!<br /> <br /> Although I already bought the 2E core book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:12:39-07:00","id":1132264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1132257#post1132257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ah, well that's a nice piece of information to have. Thank you!<br /> <br /> Although I already bought the 2E core book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The blue book can help though. I am currently running an Ordo Dracul chronicle and without the Blue Book I wouldn't know what to do in regards to them investigating occult areas beyond auspex showing that the area is wacky.<br /> <br /> I also like to use Hurt Locker for the violent skills section of the book, and for it's rules on building organizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:18:34-07:00","id":1132269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1132257#post1132257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, well that's a nice piece of information to have. Thank you!<br /> <br /> Although I already bought the 2E core book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Chronicles of Darkness has a lot of cool extra systems as well as some merits that aren't available in the other lines, if you/your ST choose to use them. Just note that some were excluded for a reason, and use your best judgment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:25:18-07:00","id":1132273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1132264#post1132264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The blue book can help though. I am currently running an Ordo Dracul chronicle and without the Blue Book I wouldn't know what to do in regards to them investigating occult areas beyond auspex showing that the area is wacky.<br /> <br /> I also like to use Hurt Locker for the violent skills section of the book, and for it's rules on building organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the blue book has a lot of relevance to the other game lines. While the books are complete in themselves they lack a <i>lot</i> of material that fortunately gets elucidated in the blue book. For example, how normal humans work, how psychic powers work, general supernatural stuff other than the whatever the core game line covers. Basically it adds a ton to your game if you choose to use it, and the idea in this thread that it's irrelevant to the other 2e core books is not accurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:36:24-07:00","id":1132279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1132269#post1132269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chronicles of Darkness has a lot of cool extra systems as well as some merits that aren't available in the other lines, if you/your ST choose to use them. Just note that some were excluded for a reason, and use your best judgment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I was very curious about the psionic merits when I picked it up. The one major complaint I have about the blue book is the God Machine Chronicle, but I just rule out the GM's existence anyways, so it's not an issue in game.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the whole GM involvement is the major reason I have no interest in picking up Demon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But on the topic of Cruac, it also takes anywhere between 1 to 5 hours of preparation before you can properly cast these rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:37:55-07:00","id":1132280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1132273#post1132273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the blue book has a lot of relevance to the other game lines. While the books are complete in themselves they lack a <i>lot</i> of material that fortunately gets elucidated in the blue book. For example, how normal humans work, how psychic powers work, general supernatural stuff other than the whatever the core game line covers. Basically it adds a ton to your game if you choose to use it, and the idea in this thread that it's irrelevant to the other 2e core books is not accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I typically always allow blue book 2e material. If I'm going to draw from it to create horrors for my chronicle, and so that I know how vampires might be able to interact with ephemeral entities (I know it isn't important to most vampire chronicles and it was excluded from vampire 2e for the intended purpose of vampires not interacting with the supernatural community at large, but running an Ordo Dracul chronicle without these things feels a little overwhelming).<br /> <br /> For willpower though, I generally try to give full willpower back on time skips. I've played characters where even though in game a week of time has passed I haven't gotten any new willpower while everyone else had their's refreshed; it irked me a little.<br /> <br /> I also try to run scenes that offer players the chance to make use of their Dirge and Mask; it makes things a little easier on that end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:38:06-07:00","id":1132281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1132273#post1132273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the idea in this thread that it's irrelevant to the other 2e core books is not accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol.<br /> <br /> You can't use a ChroD rule to say that a rule that was intentionally left out of Vampire should actually totally be there because it's in the blue book. That's what's being presented in this thread (as result of you making that argument), and it is 100% accurate. That kind of argument only made sense in 1E when the other lines <i>required</i> the blue book.<br /> <br /> No one is saying the content is irrelevant to the setting at large. We're saying stop trying to justify shoehorning a rule in that was intentionally excluded just because it's in a different gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:38:40-07:00","id":1132282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130240-willpower-cost-for-cruac-too?p=1132273#post1132273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the idea in this thread that it's irrelevant to the other 2e core books is not accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or existent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All the gamelines act as supplements to each other, by virtue of the shared setting and rules systems. The blue books are especially useful for all the other gamlines due to the non-splat specific subsystems, additions and setting pieces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}